    Remove queries from the asset manager (#6689)
    
    Fixes #5966.
    
    Removes all query related code from the asset manager. This means this
    asset manager cannot be accessed via queries anymore. Instead, the asset
    manager is exposing new methods which can be used instead.
    
    What this boils down to is dumbing down the asset manager. The query
    language we used was powerful but complex. In removing it, we lose the
    power to create whatever query we want or need on a dime. Now, if there
    is something you want to do with the asset manager but there is no
    method for it, that method will have to be written first.
    On the other hand, writing new methods should now be a lot easier. Named
    queries are less powerful, but comparatively easy to understand.
    Therefore accessing and working with the asset manager should be easier
    now.
    
    This also allows us to get rid of the query-dsl dependency, which
    hopefully makes upgrading other depdencies easier.
    
    ### How to test this patch
    
    Do whatever you can think of that would affect assets. Mostly this will
    be running workflows, but creativity is encouraged.
    
    
